# Lore.Land Projection
# The reader's projection as one Spw spell: the source every surface reads,
# shown on the page, editable, and passable as a link (book/scripts/modules/projection.mjs).
#>lore_land_surfaces_projection
#:surface #!mechanic
#:layer #!pragmatics
#:status #!seeded

~<rationale>{
  The book is one canon projected many ways: a lens, a cover, a room's light,
  an edition, what a reader's carries did. Until now those were settings in
  different drawers. Said as one Spw expression they become a thing a reader
  can read, change, and pass along, and the grammar becomes the projection's
  source rather than its decoration. Each line says where it came from, so a
  reader can always see why their page reads the way it does.
}

^"spell"{
  .note: "@reader{ … } — one line per clause; the chapter shows it under 'Read this way because…' with each line's source (yours · this visit's · your carries' · the book's own)"
  lens: "=lens[boon|bane|bone|balanced] or =genre{ boon: 50 bane: 30 bone: 20 } — the reading lens (lens-control.mjs weights)"
  audience: "=audience[pg|pg13] — what this copy shows; pg13 only once the late table and the household allow it; a spell from a link can only lower it"
  room_binding_edition: "=room[day|dusk|lamp] · =binding[rag|glass|salt|ember|slate|starfield] · =edition[…] — story directions (story-directions.mjs)"
  switches: "=with[…] · =without[…]"
  carries: "~carries{ c6: bane held · c14: boon } — what each carried chapter leans, and which the mimes hold (pie-carries.mjs)"
  measures: "%carries{ carried: 2 held: 1 won_back: 0 } — recorded measures use %, the measure sigil: counted, never chosen, never set by a link"
  plain: "!plain[carries] — read without the carries' lean (from a link: this visit only)"
  ground: ".chapter[15] — where it is being read"
  integration: "^projects[chapter, game, folio_value] — what the projection is bound into"
}

^"orthogonality"{
  .status: "proposed reading, 2026-11-10; the mechanics named are live"
  claim: "The story and the lanes are at right angles. A carry cannot change what happened in the book, and a chapter cannot change the rules of the lanes. Because neither can move the other, each can cast a shadow on the other without either being overwritten, and that shadow is the projection."
  why_right_angles: "The figure in plain lines crosses every scene at ninety degrees (story-boonhonk trope_physics). The game does the same to the book: present, consequential, and not aligned with its direction. A game that could rewrite the plot would make the plot a score."
  lanes_onto_story: "lean (the reading weighs a little toward how the carry went) · mimes (pie words go quiet) · margins (a rumour retold with what was done) · what the people remember, on their cards"
  story_onto_lanes: "rooms (the chord the land sings) · rumours heard, said in the lanes · a lens or a chapter's lean heard as the key · chapters set aside, stepped over · people kept apart, kept apart there too · where the book has two pies in a room, the second answers the first"
  rule: "A shadow never moves the thing that cast it. Variant zero stays in the page, and the prophecy always holds."
  escape: "This is also why the lanes can be for getting away. Nothing you do there is the book, so nothing there is homework. The reasons for each person live on their card, folded, off the lanes."
  &reasons: ~".spw/surfaces/reasons.spw"
  &tropes: ~".spw/surfaces/tropes.spw#tropes"
}

^"passing_it_along"{
  link: "?spell=<the spell> — on arrival it becomes this visit's story directions (never saved as the reader's own unless they keep it), ?audience=pg (lower only) and ?plain=carries (this visit)"
  safety: "a spell from a link can never raise the audience, set a measure, or overwrite the reader's own settings"
}

^"next"{
  audience_gate: "PG-13-leaning themes live only in tagged variants (=audience[pg13]) with a PG twin that book:check requires; they open through the late table (an in-world invitation after Book One, answered with a question whoever holds the book answers easily) and a household key (set in the binder's room, lockable with a word only its keeper knows)"
  folio_value: "a folio's ask is formula-only: the tier's working ask (October drop as Seeds, $35) moved by the play spell within −25% to +15%; play arrives as % measures (%carried, %satisfied, %wonders, %held, %won_back, %foils…); each original records %fulfill[p], the chance it can be delivered as it is — fulfilling an original is the premium form, otherwise the order is the maker's interpretation of its inspirational process, or a print; the spell recomputes under the published policy and an auditor checks the play is a reachable game state, so the reason for a price can be discussed and checked"
}
